Less white in the text
=====================

Body text was #d9d9d9 — a neutral near-white — so the window read as white type on black with green
trim, instead of a green-on-black terminal. Both tones move toward the palette:

  --text   #d9d9d9 -> #b7cfbe     a pale grey-green, still high enough contrast on #040d08
  --muted  #7fb18c -> #82a891     one step greener, so secondary text belongs to the same family

Contrast against the background stays above 7:1 for body text, so this is tone, not a legibility
trade. The accent (#02d63a) and the headings that use it are unchanged — the point is that the accent
is the only thing shouting.
diff -Naur a/resources/ui/app.css b/resources/ui/app.css
